WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 078. A STUDY TRAVELS. EVIDENCE CAN FRAY.. Translation needs an evidence-preservation protocol, even when every record and audience is fictional.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
FIX THE TRUTH ANCHORS. SOURCE · QUALITY · CLAIM · POPULATION · OUTCOME. The source type, supported claim, studied population, comparison, and outcome remain fixed.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
KEEP THE LIMITS. LIMITATIONS · UNCERTAINTY · AS-OF DATE. Audience-friendly language cannot upgrade source quality, erase uncertainty, or extend the evidence beyond its bounds.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
ATTACH AUDIENCE CAVEATS. PUBLIC · CLINICAL EDUCATOR · POLICY · PRODUCT · ADVOCATE. The explanation adapts to its reader while audience-specific caveats travel with it.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
BOUND THE RESULT. TRANSLATION IS NOT ADVICE OR PROOF. Synthetic evidence only; no patient, product, current-law, legal, clinical, diagnosis, treatment, dosage, safety, effectiveness, or compliance claim.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. CHANGE THE LANGUAGE. KEEP THE EVIDENCE INTACT.. EVIDENCE TRANSLATION WORKS WHEN SOURCE QUALITY, CLAIM, POPULATION, EXPOSURE, COMPARISON, OUTCOME, LIMITS, UNCERTAINTY, DATE, AND CAVEATS STAY CONNECTED.

